GOAL_HDR = ["Your goal (your words)", "What the research actually finds moves it", "Track elements that serve it", "Breath / body practices (from the library)", "Beyond the track: the practices with the best evidence", "Evidence", "Plain truth"]
GOALS = [
    ["Open the third eye / pineal gland", "The pineal responds to light, not sound; the 'third eye' as experienced (brow pressure, inner light) comes from upward gaze (Shambhavi), retention-induced entoptic phosphenes (Jyoti mudrā), frontal-sinus vibration from humming, and theta-stage imagery. Melatonin rhythm is strengthened by darkness at night and bright light by day.",
     "Ajna stage: 6 Hz beat, seven-vowel ladder, bowl ladder; bhramari in the Threshold; the 963 Hz bowl as ceremony.", "#3 Bhramari, #18 Jyoti mudrā, #30 Shambhavi mudrā, #14 inner-sound listening, #16 Hong-Sau gaze.", "Strict light hygiene (dark room, no screens 2–3 h before, morning daylight); regular sleep; daily 20 min of the Ajna techniques.", "Brow/inner-light phenomena: traditional, reliably reproducible. Pineal change by sound: none.", "You will get the experiences the traditions describe. The gland itself is not touched by sound."],
    ["Align with the universe", "The measurable 'alignment' available to a body is coherence among its own oscillators: breath–heart–blood-pressure resonance at 0.1 Hz, breath-locked attention, circadian alignment to the solar day. Schumann 'tuning' has no demonstrated biological coupling.", "Breath pacer at 6/min; 7.83 / 14.1 Hz plateaus as symbolic anchors; the whole track in pure ratios from one tone.", "#46 coherent breathing, #27 2:1, #42 Jesus Prayer / #41 dhikr rate, #13 So'ham.", "10–20 min daily coherent breathing (HRV biofeedback if you can); fixed wake time and morning light.", "Strong for HRV coherence; none for cosmic coupling.", "Alignment inside the body is real and trainable; alignment with Earth/cosmos frequencies is a metaphor."],
    ["Divine wisdom / insight", "Insight experiences cluster in theta-rich, low-executive states (hypnagogia, deep absorption) and in the alpha 'open focus' state; creativity gains from 10 Hz/40 Hz beats appear in some individuals (low eye-blink rate); long-term meditation changes gamma synchrony. The content of insight is yours.", "Descent (SATS window), Drum Gate journey, No-Time with gamma cues, Crown.", "#39 Ānāpānasati (the structure), #44 Vijñāna Bhairava pauses, #25 count-down, Open-Focus space questions in the guide.", "Daily sitting practice (mindfulness/open monitoring) — the only intervention with large-sample evidence for attention and insight-related measures; journaling immediately after sessions.", "Moderate for state access; individual for content.", "The track opens the door reliably; what walks through is not guaranteed."],
    ["Manifestation", "The documented mechanism is psychological: rehearsing a desired state in the hypnagogic window (Neville's SATS, Yoga Nidra sankalpa, sports mental imagery) changes attention, expectancy, mood and subsequent behaviour. No mechanism exists for intention acting on external probability.", "Threshold intention slot (3:00–4:00); Descent quiet window (6:00–11:00) with the 68-s bowl marker; Return sankalpa.", "#21 three-part breath on the swell for the statement; #17 kriya pranayama around the scene; #25 count-down to stay conscious.", "Same scene, same time, daily, for 4–8 weeks; write the scene first; act on the openings that appear.", "Moderate for imagery/expectancy effects on behaviour and performance; none for external effects.", "Manifestation works on you; through you it can work on the world."],
    ["Mastery over vibration, energy, frequency", "You own several oscillators and can train them: breath rate and ratio, HRV resonance, vocal fundamental and overtones (toning, overtone singing), EEG rhythm bias via attention and entrainment, circadian phase via light, body temperature via tummo. 'Energy' sensations are CO₂, blood-flow and interoceptive events you can learn to produce at will.", "Every layer is a handle: pacer (0.1 Hz), beats (2–14 Hz), gamma cues (40 Hz), hum (136/272 Hz), overtone drone.", "#3 Bhramari and vowel toning, #4/#5 fast techniques (seated), #32 tummo, #46 coherent breathing, #17 kriya pranayama.", "Learn overtone singing (sygyt-style harmonic isolation) and daily toning; HRV biofeedback app with a finger sensor; cold/heat exposure with tummo breathing.", "Strong for breath/HRV/voice; moderate for temperature; none for external 'energy'.", "This is the most achievable of the goals, in the literal sense."],
    ["Mind operating beyond human levels", "Measurable cognitive gains from entrainment are modest (g ≈ 0.4): working memory with 40 Hz, attentional-blink reduction with gamma beats, vigilance with beta beats, and only in some people. Large gains come from sleep, exercise, long-term meditation and deliberate practice.", "40 Hz cues; 14.1 Hz SMR return; alpha stack.", "#1 Nadi Shodhana before cognitive work, #49 physiological sigh for arousal control.", "Sleep regularity; aerobic exercise; 40 Hz light+sound sessions are being trialled clinically for cognition; daily meditation.", "Moderate (small effects).", "Expect sharper, calmer, not superhuman."],
    ["Travel between dimensions and realms (OBE)", "The states exist and are reproducible: hypnagogic OBE, Monroe's vibrational state, shamanic journey imagery, lucid dreaming. They are generated by the brain (TPJ/vestibular conflict, sleep paralysis, REM intrusion) and are experienced as travel. Wake-back-to-bed timing, lying still, darkness and journey instructions raise the rate dramatically.", "Drum Gate (journey), No-Time (vibrational state: 2.13 Hz floor, 0.2 Hz surge, alpha stack, gamma cues), call-back.", "#12 kevala kumbhaka (allow), #44 pauses, #25 count-down (lucidity thread), Monroe's 'smooth and speed the vibrations'.", "WBTB 2–3 nights a week with the track; lucid-dream training (MILD, reality checks, dream journal); core-shamanic journey practice with stated intentions.", "Strong for the phenomenology; the experiences are not verified as external events.", "You can learn to go there often. 'There' is in here."],
    ["Travel in time / places in time", "Monroe's Focus 15 'no time' is a reproducible state of timelessness and of vivid memory/imagery that practitioners interpret as past/future access; no verified instance of information from the future exists (remote-viewing programmes were closed for lack of operational value).", "No-Time stage (2.13 Hz, stilled breath, thunders), Crown clear-light return.", "#44 pauses, #35 embryonic breathing, #12.", "Memory reconsolidation work and imagination training in the hypnagogic window; keep records and check them against reality — the only honest test.", "None for information transfer; strong for the state.", "The state of no-time is available; time travel is not a claim this project makes."],
    ["Growth over weeks", "Daily 30–60 min for 4–8 weeks is the dose in every longitudinal pilot (anxiety, quality of life); the adaptation phase (vivid dreams, drowsiness) is days 1–7.", "Full session daily or the 15-min version twice.", "The protocol sheets.", "A weekly 0–10 log (calm, clarity, sleep, discomfort); review at 4 and 8 weeks.", "Weak–moderate (small studies).", "Keep the log; it is the instrument."],
]

